        "description": "<div class=\"field field--name-body field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden\"><div class=\"field__items\"><div class=\"field__item even\"><p><span>The </span><a href=\"https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/2026/06/tell-congress-just-say-no-no-fakes\"><span>NO FAKES Act</span></a><span> is supposed to target harmful AI-generated impersonations. But in reality, it will <a href=\"https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/2026/06/tell-congress-just-say-no-no-fakes\">make it easier to suppress</a> commentary, satire, and other lawful speech. That's why EFF has signed a </span><a href=\"https://cdt.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/NO-FAKES-Summer-2026_FINAL-1.pdf\"><span>letter</span></a><span> urging the Senate Judiciary Committee not to advance the bill in its current form.</span></p>\n<p class=\"take-action\"><a href=\"https://act.eff.org/action/tell-congress-just-say-no-to-no-fakes\">Take action</a></p>\n<p class=\"take-explainer\"><a href=\"https://act.eff.org/action/tell-congress-throw-out-the-no-fakes-act-and-start-",
